From: Chaos Ruler <zmelumian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Steam: keep the pad settings across boots, art for installed games

Steam keys controller settings by serial and InputPlumber's virtual
DualSense gets a new one each boot: copy the newest settings to today's
(steam-pad-prefs.sh). steam-art.py fetches covers, logos, screenshots and
details for the installed games in the background.
---
--- a/projects/ROCKNIX/packages/emulators/standalone/steam/scripts/start_steam_arm64.sh
+++ b/projects/ROCKNIX/packages/emulators/standalone/steam/scripts/start_steam_arm64.sh
@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@
 
 steam_ensure_fex_config_template
 steam_prepare_storage_and_vdf
+# Asgard: the pad's Steam settings survive InputPlumber's per-boot serial; art for the installed games.
+/usr/share/asgard/steam-pad-prefs.sh
+( python3 /usr/share/asgard/steam-art.py >/var/log/steam-art.log 2>&1 & )
 steam_load_es_thunk_settings "$@"
 steam_apply_lsfg_settings
 steam_apply_fps_limit
